=== CO3 Q7: TELEMEDICINE PLATFORM PROTOCOL CHOICE FROM FIRST PRINCIPLES ===
Stage 1 — Traffic Requirements (Unreliable 4G: 100-300 ms RTT, up to 5% loss):
  - Live Video Consult      : Delay <= 150 ms 1-way | Loss Tolerates <= 1-2% loss  | Order Real-time / drop stale | Sec DTLS/SRTP
  - Patient Records & X-Ray : Delay <= 5-15 s total | Loss 0% loss (100% reliable) | Order Strictly ordered | Sec TLS 1.3
  - Doctor-Patient Chat     : Delay <= 500 ms       | Loss 0% loss                 | Order Strictly ordered | Sec TLS 1.3
  - Hospital Service DNS    : Delay <= 100 ms       | Loss Retryable               | Order N/A              | Sec DNSSEC / DoH

Stage 2 — Protocol Comparison & 64 KB TCP Window Limit:
  - Max TCP throughput with 64 KB window @ 300 ms RTT : 1.748 Mbps
  - 20 MB X-ray transfer time without Window Scaling  : >= 91.6 s (exceeds target!)
  - Selected Stack:
      * Live Video    -> RTP/UDP + SRTP (no TCP HoL blocking) + FEC / adaptive bitrate
      * X-Ray & Chat  -> HTTP/3 over QUIC (or TCP+TLS 1.3 with RFC 7323 Window Scaling >= 512 KB + BBR)
      * DNS & QoS     -> TTL 300s cached DNS + DiffServ EF (video), AF21 (chat), AF11 (X-ray bulk)

Stage 3 — Socket Implementation & Verification (4G: 200 ms RTT scaled, 5% loss):
  - Clean link (0% loss)       : delivered 32,768 B | retransmits=0 | time=35.58 ms
  - Unreliable 4G (5% loss)    : delivered 32,768 B | retransmits=0 | time=2.19 ms

Stage 4 — Design Defence & 5G Upgrade Impact:
  - UDP/SRTP prevents 5% 4G loss from freezing video; HTTP/3+QUIC + Window Scaling prevents 64 KB BDP stall on X-rays.
  - Upgraded to 5G (<20 ms RTT, <0.1% loss): X-ray throughput jumps 15x even with 64 KB window; video jitter drops <5 ms.

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: Commercial Video-Consultation SaaS ---
  - Key due-diligence questions: (1) P95 glass-to-glass latency & SFU PoP proximity; (2) FEC/concealment at 5% loss;
    (3) End-to-end encryption, HIPAA/DISHA data residency, BAA & zero PHI logging.
